# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# The build the artifact needs nothing to produce, but `npm install` is optional and only
# ever for the test suite's validator cross-check (README, "Build and test").
node_modules/
*.log

# The BUILD OUTPUT. `node build.js` writes dist/trip-planner.html here, and the GitHub Pages
# deployment publishes exactly this folder (.github/workflows/pages.yml). It is ignored because the
# artifact is a compiled result: a repository that carries its own build ships a second copy of the
# app, and the copy is the one people open — so a commit that edited src/ without rebuilding would
# publish a file that disagrees with its own source, silently. `node build.js` reproduces it from a
# bare checkout with nothing installed.
dist/

# A sample interchange file, used while developing the mappers, not part of the app
trip-data.json
